  "notes": "County, cash basis, governmental only (no business-type funds). Governmental receipts/disbursements from Statement of Receipts, Disbursements and Changes in Fund Balances (p4), Total Governmental Funds column. Taxes 7,694,964 split into property, motor vehicle, lodging and other using the general receipts on the Statement of Activities (p2); inheritance tax is its own printed line on p4. Intergovernmental is as printed. Local (2,820,650) split using the Statement of Activities (p2): charges for services 1,100,842, interest income 305,751, miscellaneous 1,414,057 (other, review). Beginning cash = beginning fund balance 10,636,802 and ending cash = ending fund balance 7,856,312 as the statement rolls forward (includes investments and restricted amounts: cash 1,441,154, investments 3,795,855, restricted cash 2,128,659, restricted investments 490,644 per p1); investments not separately listed as informational. Transfers in and out both 9,206,553 (net zero). Bond proceeds 1,304,249. Reconciles: 10,636,802 + 17,368,095 - 21,452,834 + 9,206,553 - 9,206,553 + 1,304,249 = 7,856,312. Balance sheet is the cash-basis Statement of Net Position (p1), governmental activities (only column); no liabilities. Detail: the General Fund combining statement (p5) has two columns, General Fund and Inheritance Tax Fund, totalling Total General Fund (receipts 9,560,696). The General Fund column (receipts 9,133,334, disbursements 7,220,518) is recorded from the more detailed p14 budget schedule (double counting avoided); its function groupings differ from the statement's function columns on p4 (e.g. schedule general government 3,943,829 vs statement 3,694,072 plus capital outlay 332,110) though total disbursements 7,220,518 tie. The Inheritance Tax Fund column (p5: inheritance tax 427,362, no disbursements, transfers in 1,622,537, transfers out 1,883,166) is recorded separately as fund 'Inheritance Tax'; it is not on p14. The General Fund 'Taxes' line (6,548,198) has no printed breakdown by tax type, so it is taxes (unlabeled). Detail for the other major funds from their budget schedules (pp15-18; disbursements printed as a single line; Highway Allocation Bond Fund split into principal 355,000 and interest 59,226 from p4). Nonmajor funds (more than 6) recorded using Total Nonmajor Funds column (p13); individual fund pages 6-12 not itemized. Transfer cross-check: all transfers in and out net to zero across funds (including the Inheritance Tax Fund column) and none are embedded in spending lines. Noxious Weed placed under streets/highways because printed under the Public Works heading. Read pages 1-18 of 18"
}